Jesse Meyer wrote:
> Today, someone in #nethack (freenode) asked if eating a wand of
> teleportation lead to teleportitis.
> 
> The answer is (of course) no, but it lead to me considering what would
> happen if eating wands could lead to intrinsics.

I think it's a great idea. All that stored up energy has to go 
somewhere, after all.

> A short list of possible effects:

No effects in any case if the wand is empty.

> enlightenment:	Same as !oEnlightenment.
> make invisible: 	Invisibility.
> slow monster: 	Speed loss.
> speed monster: 	Speed gain.

Good. These effects all happen when you zap the wand, so there's little 
change.

> undead turning: 	Polymorph into a random undead creature.

This could conflict with polymorph control (which you probably have if 
you're eating wands).

> cold:		Cold damage, chance of fire resistance.
> fire: 	Fire damage, chance of cold resistance.
> lightning: 	shock damage, chance of shock resistance.

The chance should go up with the number of charges -- but so should the 
damage.
  	
> sleep: 	Fall asleep.
> polymorph: 	Same as !oPolymorph
> cancellation:	Lose one intrinsic (same as gremlin attack).

Agreed.
  	
> death: 	Insta-Death.

I'm surprised this isn't already implemented.

> light: 	Same as !ofLevitation (makes you _light_).

'sgreat. I love it.

> teleportation:	Teleportitis, chance of teleportation control if blessed.

I'd make the chance of teleport control very small.

> magic missile, striking:	 minor damage. 	
> nothing: 	no effect.

[wands and effects switched] Fair enough.

> small chance of max pw increase/pw increase:
> 	digging, locking, opening, probing, secret door detection, 
> 	create monster, wishing.

As the number of charges increases, the chance of a magical explosion in 
your stomach (for lotsa damage) should increase.

